# AP2 - Fault injection: artificial bounce ("scratch test"), debounced firmware
# Date:      2026-11-07
# Firmware:  same as ap2_acceptance.log (DEBOUNCE_MS = 10 ms)
# Procedure: jumper wire on GND scratched across GPIO 15 to create many
#            bounce edges; afterwards one normal press so the serial line is current
# Reference: PulseView, CH0 = GPIO 15, 8 MHz, Counter decoder on falling edges
# Expected:  PulseView count >> raw edges > press
#
# Result (filter funnel):
#   93 falling edges on the pin     (PulseView counter)
#   29 reached the ISR              (raw edges)  -> 64 masked within 10 ms windows
#   19 confirmed as press           (press)      -> 10 rejected, pin HIGH after T
#   -> PASS: bounce filter is effective
#
# Limitations:
#   - Comparison only valid if capture and firmware counter started together.
#   - raw edges is printed only on the next press; checks after the last
#     press are not visible in the log.
#   - Scratching has no "correct" press count; this test proves filtering,
#     counting accuracy is proven by ap2_acceptance.log.

---- Opened the serial port /dev/tty.usbmodem144301 ----
press 1, raw edges 2
press 2, raw edges 2
press 3, raw edges 3
press 4, raw edges 4
press 5, raw edges 6
press 6, raw edges 8
press 7, raw edges 10
press 8, raw edges 12
